sequenceDiagram
  %% Current flow: stage 2 of the command development pipeline. A task runs in a copy of its Project's default container Instance. Acquire it before prep when prep runs there, then reuse that copy for build and proof. A nested-fleet Project gives it its own Gateway, app-dev and app-prod containers. Task start and completion details belong to docs/cli/task/start.mmd.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: development pipeline stage 2 · task copy and nested fleet
  %% kind: pipeline.2-development-environment
  autonumber
  %% lane AG icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane CP icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  %% lane NT icon=server pill=fleet tone=amber
  participant AG as Author<br/>agent or person
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>create · complete
  participant CP as Task copy<br/>container Instance
  participant NT as Nested fleet<br/>Gateway · 2 Nodes
  opt the task has not started
    AG->>GW: Start the task<br/>task:start GROUP
    %%> Requirements:
    %%> - the task is todo and its Project's default Instance is a container; Orbit command development uses a Project with a nested fleet
    Note over GW: Record the task copy<br/>branch · owner · create
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - binds the copy to the task and admits instance.create in one transaction; task copies take no CI place
    GW->>SW: Create and complete<br/>operation-instance-create
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - starts the normal Instance clone flow after the transaction commits; instance.complete finishes setup after create
    SW->>CP: Clone the default seed<br/>workspace · task branch
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - copies the container and its inner volume when present; the copy owns its workspace and fleet
    SW->>CP: Complete the copy<br/>database · Processes · fleet
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - makes the copy active only after its setup and nested fleet are ready
  end
  alt the copy is active
    SW-->>GW: Copy ready<br/>task running
    GW-->>AG: Development environment<br/>copy active
    loop build the whole feature
      AG->>CP: Edit and test<br/>one feature branch
      CP->>NT: Exercise the real path<br/>CLI · API · effect
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - nested Nodes mount the copy's checkout; apply migrations and service changes before API checks
      %%> - codify manual changes and test the full end result here, not through a sequence of releases
    end
    Note over AG,NT: Run stage 3 in this copy<br/>before opening the PR
  else create or completion fails
    SW--xGW: Setup failed<br/>failed step · Operation
    GW--xAG: Environment not ready<br/>follow task:start recovery
    %%> Result:
    %%> - no build or proof starts on an incomplete copy; task:start owns create retries, safe removal and completion recovery
  end
